/*!
 * \mainpage TFELMathEnzyme Documentation
 * 
 * \section intro_sec Introduction
 * 
 * <b>TFELMathEnzyme</b> is a C++ library that extends the 
 * <a href="https://thelfer.github.io/tfel/web/tfel-math.html">TFEL/Math</a>
 * library with automatic differentiation capabilities powered by the 
 * <a href="https://enzyme.mit.edu/">Enzyme</a> project. This integration enables
 * users to compute derivatives of mathematical functions and callables automatically,
 * leveraging both forward and reverse mode automatic differentiation.
 * 
 * \section features_sec Key Features
 * 
 * - <b>Automatic Differentiation</b>: Compute derivatives of callables and free 
 *   functions using Enzyme's forward and reverse mode AD.
 * - <b>TFEL/Math Integration</b>: Seamlessly works with TFEL's mathematical objects 
 *   and utilities.
 * - <b>Header-Only Library</b>: Lightweight and easy to integrate into existing 
 *   projects.
 * - <b>Modern C++</b>: Written in C++20 with extensive use of templates, concepts, 
 *   and type traits.
 * - <b>Comprehensive Testing</b>: Includes unit tests for all major functionality.
 * 
 * \section usecases_sec Use Cases
 * 
 * TFELMathEnzyme is particularly useful for:
 * - Scientific computing applications requiring automatic differentiation
 * - Optimization algorithms that need gradient computations
 * - Machine learning applications
 * - Engineering applications, especially in material modeling and finite element analysis
 * 
 * \section getting_started_sec Getting Started
 * 
 * \subsection install_subsec Installation
 * 
 * See the <a href="https://github.com/thelfer/TFELMathEnzyme/blob/master/INSTALL.md">INSTALL.md</a>
 * file for detailed installation instructions.
 * 
 * \subsection basic_example_subsec Basic Example
 * 
 * The following example demonstrates how to compute the derivative of a simple function:
 * 
 * \code
 * #include <TFEL/Math/Enzyme/computeDerivative.hxx>
 * #include <TFEL/Math/Enzyme/Variable.hxx>
 * 
 * using namespace tfel::math::enzyme;
 * 
 * // Define a simple function
 * auto square = [](double x) { return x * x; };
 * 
 * // Compute its derivative at x = 2.0
 * auto derivative = computeDerivative<Mode::FORWARD, 0>(square, 2.0);
 * // derivative now contains 4.0 (2 * 2.0)
 * \endcode
 * 
 * \section architecture_sec Architecture Overview
 * 
 * \subsection core_components_subsec Core Components
 * 
 * The library is organized into several key components:
 * 
 * <b>Main Functionality:</b>
 * - <b>computeDerivative</b>: Computes derivatives of callables or free functions 
 *   with respect to specified variables. Supports both forward and reverse mode 
 *   differentiation.
 * - <b>fwddiff</b>: Computes the increment of a callable given variable values and 
 *   their increments using Enzyme's forward mode AD.
 * - <b>Variable Utilities</b>: Provides utilities for handling variables in 
 *   differentiation, including the VariableConcept, VariableValueAndIncrement 
 *   structure, and helper functions.
 * - <b>Derivative Functions</b>: Higher-level abstractions for derivative computation 
 *   including getDerivativeFunction, getForwardModeDerivativeFunction, and 
 *   getReverseModeDerivativeFunction.
 * 
 * <b>Internal Utilities:</b>
 * - Type traits for working with Enzyme and TFEL types
 * - Function utilities for handling function pointers and callables
 * - Low-level integration with Enzyme's AD capabilities
 * 
 * \subsection namespace_org_subsec Namespace Organization
 * 
 * All functionality is provided within the <b>tfel::math::enzyme</b> namespace.
 * Internal utilities are in the <b>tfel::math::enzyme::internals</b> namespace.
 * 
 * \section dependencies_sec Dependencies
 * 
 * - <b>C++20 Compiler</b>: Required for modern C++ features
 * - <b>LLVM 18+</b>: Enzyme requires LLVM 18 or later
 * - <b>Enzyme</b>: Automatic differentiation library
 * - <b>TFEL/Math</b>: Mathematical library from the TFEL project
 * 
 * \section project_structure_sec Project Structure
 * 
 * The project is organized as follows:
 * 
 * - <b>include/TFEL/Math/Enzyme/</b>: Public headers containing the main library functionality
 * - <b>src/</b>: Library definition (INTERFACE target)
 * - <b>tests/</b>: Unit tests for all major functionality
 * 
 * \section additional_info_sec Additional Information
 * 
 * - <a href="https://github.com/thelfer/TFELMathEnzyme">GitHub Repository</a>
 * - <a href="https://github.com/thelfer/TFELMathEnzyme/blob/master/README.md">README.md</a>
 * - <a href="https://github.com/thelfer/TFELMathEnzyme/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>
 * - <a href="https://enzyme.mit.edu/">Enzyme Project</a>
 * - <a href="https://thelfer.github.io/tfel/web/tfel-math.html">TFEL/Math Documentation</a>
 * 
